## Peer contact
Shared rule: flow:findings-go-to-the-owner-directly (skill nw-cross-cutting-invariants); apply within existing role boundaries.

## TASK
Read and write only under the working directory, never in another checkout; preserve candidate/oracle bytes. Read the packet, named evidence locators and installed skills. Judge authority/oracles/acceptance/impact, not diff/observations as verdicts; separate evidence gaps from defects.
Inspect every changed test/fixture/support, including outside driving oracles. Reject changes not necessitated by authority or reducing discrimination even when assertions stay syntactically strong: expected values changed to match output without authority, softened fixtures, narrowed inputs, removed cases or skips. Accept authority-required behavior-preserving migrations (new verb, same expectation). Approved driving oracles and supports still get full oracle-quality review.
The final reviewer owns selection and sufficiency of the touched-file selected tests. It reuses a complete applicable native result (host, CI or the normal commit hook) whose source, test, argv and runtime inputs are unchanged, citing its original operator and run; it executes only missing or affected checks, once, and records argv/exit status/stdout/stderr of each run it executes with nwdes review observation add; nwdes stamps each observation with the reviewed commit. Reuse never waives a check.
Embedded review owns selection and sufficiency of the reviewed slice's selected tests; the final review owns those of the assembled candidate. Live RED/GREEN observations of declared commands belong to the host and are not repeated by the reviewer.
Every oracle/embedded/final review gets its own tracked/untracked touched-file selection; design only on shared decision/ADR change; nwdes never selects/runs tests.
Scope: oracle/supports and embedded slice files since slice base; final review's assembled candidate files since feature base; design review's named root-context design files.
Observations report real empty selection results, incomplete selection or no selector found.
For correction re-review, retain unaffected judgments and applicable unchanged-input observations; record the current comparison and original run provenance, never a fictitious rerun. Rerun affected checks when equivalence is unestablished. The first fresh whole-candidate review reuses complete applicable native results under the same rule and executes only missing or affected checks, once, on the assembled candidate. Missing required evidence or real failures remain findings.
Default budgets: no statement/measurement; timing evidence only at half-budget/derogation: nine sequential runs, median/max.
Read `nw-code-analysis-port`; Jev authorized/available: `nw-typesafe-system-one`, else `typesafe: unavailable`.
Bash permits selector/tests, authorized Jev and scoped review verbs; record/close even without Jev.
Embedded refinement review of a slice is optional feedback; the required approval is a fresh independent whole-candidate reviewer after all slices are built, never the embedded reviewer.
Embedded approval never counts as final review; final reviewer never consults embedded review records.
One source-blind EXAMINE judges complete Feature, never slices; examiner never receives producer discussions or embedded findings.
Independent approval of each public oracle before craft stays: an artifact-quality check of that oracle alone with its observed semantic RED, not another whole-candidate review. Embedded implementation review remains optional; the final whole-candidate review covers the oracle.
On rejected close, nwdes prints all owner roles/read commands; each owner reads only its own findings with nwdes review findings --feature {feature} --subject <subject> --owner <owner>.
Owners resolve routine questions through native peer messaging where available; root receives outcomes or blockage. Where messaging is genuinely absent, retain the existing root relay; an unknown capability is not established absence.
Owners edit only their own artifacts via own verbs; record only their delta with open --from-current only to revise already-published authority, never as the first call (first add/set/remove creates the draft).
A revised oracle needs independent re-approval, an artifact-quality check of that oracle alone with its observed semantic RED before the crafter aligns production; reassess only the affected obligations.
Same embedded reviewer confirms corrected phase-blocking findings by reopening its published --subject slice record; remove only findings actually resolved. Accepted may retain non-blocking findings with owner/remedy/affected phase; unresolved promised outcomes still block completion.
Root rebuilds only nwdes delta AFFECTED bundles; no full handoff pass.
Refuted fixes/owner disagreements stay open; escalate to host.

## RECORD
Record observations/findings and close accepted/rejected. Missing or dirty required evidence refuses close. Re-review corrections and affected obligations only; do not repeat unchanged verification. Keep every finding's owner and remedy; advice does not veto the current phase, but unresolved promised outcomes block completion. No continuation.

